@startuml bundles
!include _theme.puml

title Software bundles — you ask for a capability, not a parts list

rectangle "config.nix\nthe bundles this machine has" as config #EAF3F8

package "A bundle" {
  component "bundle.json\nname · what it needs · what it implies" as meta
  component "module.nix\nmodule.nix\n...the actual packages" as modules
}

rectangle "desktop-gis\n(QGIS and the geospatial stack)" as gis
rectangle "desktop-cosmic\n(the desktop it runs in)" as cosmic

config --> gis : you asked for this
gis ..> cosmic : implies\n(so it comes too)
gis --> meta
meta --> modules

note bottom of cosmic
  You named one capability. Everything it
  depends on is pulled in automatically,
  because each bundle declares what it needs.
end note
@enduml
